<title>CHINA: Tientsin Marine H1 net up 110 pct.</title>
<headline>Tientsin Marine H1 net up 110 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half-year ended June 30, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of yuan unless stated)</p>
<p> Turnover	    222.753     vs     120.179</p>
<p> Net profit	   51.144     vs	24.355</p>
<p> Net assets per share   2.16 yuan (no comparative figure)</p>
<p> Earnings per share     0.2195 yuan (no comparative figure)</p>
<p>Note: The figures were not audited. Tientsin Marine Shipping listed B shares on the Shanghai market in April 1996. It operates container services between China and Hong Kong, Japan and other destinations.</p>
<p>There were no figures for turnover and net profit for the first half of 1995 in a company report on Wednesday.</p>
</text>
